      "message": "while this is a generally okay check, the approach i\u0027d prefer to use for validations of this nature are more as follows:\n\ncreate a module, keystone/clean.py\n\nin clean you\u0027ll have some basic checks like this one, which could be done as something like\n\ndef require_length(...) \n\nor could be represented as a regex (use a \\w{min,max} style thing)\n\nThen, within that same file add specific ones like \n\ndef user_name(...):\n  do all the checks for a user name\n\ndef tenant_name(...):\n  do all the checks for a tenant name\n\nand upon entering a tenant_create one would say\n\ntenant_name \u003d clean.tenant_name(tenant[\u0027name\u0027])\n\nthrow an error if it is an unrecoverable problem, otherwise normalize appropriately and return the new value\n\n\nsome examples of this style here: http://code.google.com/p/jaikuengine/source/browse/trunk/common/clean.py",
